<title>UK: Rentokil hit by Berendsen warning.</title>
<headline>Rentokil hit by Berendsen warning.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Britain's Rentokil Initial dropped in a rising market on Monday after its Danish parent Sophus Berendsen issued a profit warning.</p>
<p>Rentokil Initial shares touched an intraday low of 410-1/2p before paring losses to trade at 413p, down 1-1/2p on the day. Just over 10 million shares had changed hands by 1333 GMT, making Rentokil London's second most-traded stock.</p>
<p>Sophus Berendsen shares dropped in Copenhagen after the company said it expected pretax earnings to fall to 145 million crowns this year from 275 million in 1995.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
